  m_Name: Job_IslandDeck
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: WoodcraftSimulator::WoodcraftSimulator.Jobs.JobDefinition
  id: island-deck-job
  displayName: Island house deck with glass railing
  description: A deck at an island house facing the sea, with a ready-made glass
    railing on its front edge (three panels, two clamps each).
  blueprint: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 65227cb9e9c33194dae3a6a9c76b98a4, type: 2}
  stockSpecies: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 3fd4be3a08bd3c74f9b6fafeb4fe74ab, type: 2}
  stockLengthMillimeters: 2400
  stockWidthMillimeters: 145
  stockThicknessMillimeters: 28
  spareBoards: 0
  tips:
  - Drive there with the van (it stands in the workshop yard). The material is delivered
    to the site; take your tools (the belt, or loaded in the van bed) and the stepladder
    if you need it.
  - Set out at the corner stake, prepare the pier spots, then build bottom up; the
    customer inspects each stage (E on the corner stake).
  - 'The glass panels come ready-made: carry one to the front edge of the deck and
    fix it with its two clamps (drill-driver).'
  - Hand the finished job over at the house door.
  payEuros: 1650
  requiresFinish: 0
